# Commit on main

This is a personal dots repo. Agents usually sit in a linked worktree (Herdr start-work, WorkTrunk). A commit on that worktree branch is easy to forget: Drew hears the fix landed, treats `~/dots` as the live tree, and the work never reaches `main`.

When asked to commit (or when the work should persist):

1. Apply the change on the main checkout at `~/dots`, on the `main` branch.
2. Commit there. Do not leave the only copy on the worktree branch.
3. If you edited files in this worktree first, copy or apply the same patch to `~/dots` before committing, then restore the worktree copy so it does not look like a second uncommitted change.

A worktree commit is allowed if Drew asks for that branch. Default is `~/dots` `main`.

This rule is only for this repo. Do not copy it to other checkouts.
